Test inputs of the corpus of cas (compare/cas/progcfg.py, compare/casold/progcfg.py)
====================================================================================

The corpus runs the original /bin/cas (under z8k-emu), the build of src/cmd/cas and the host build on the same inputs; messages, exit
status and every file written must be equal (compare/cas/case.sh). The inputs are the same every time, nothing is random.

casgen.py   opcodes(mode)   every valid opcode as decoded by host/tools/z8k.py (modes ns, ss, sl: nonsegmented, short and long segmented
                            addresses), written as source in blocks of 3000 instructions
            fuzz(mode)      operand patterns (about 1200 per mnemonic) for the mnemonics z8k.py does not decode (EPU, block
                            instructions, ...), modes ns and sl
            reljump(...)    jr, djnz, calr, ldr, jpr, callr, jp, call at 23 distances, and chains of jpr at the limit of the short form
jpr/*.s     fixed sources, each with its purpose in the comment at the top: the decision of jpr and callr (jr/calr or jp/call):
            edge_jpr, edge_callr      the edges of the short form (+256/-254 bytes, +4098/-4092 bytes), forward and backward
            dep_forward, dep_backward, back_undecided, mutual, cascade, mixed
                                      entries that jump over each other, so that the growth of one decides the others
            offsets, parity, sections the offset label+n, odd and even lengths, several sections
            operands, extern_*, operr_*   all operand forms; one error in a file (an error of this kind ends the assembly)
            old_block, old_max, old_label the special rules of the old cas (compare/casold only, OLD_ENTBLK 176 at a {, OLD_ENTMAX 255,
                                          a jpr at its label): the shipped cas stops on old_max with "Not enough core"
Every jpr/NAME.s is assembled nonsegmented and with a .seg in front (jpr:NAME) and with the options -l -d -r -t -i -m -v -^ (opt:NAME).
The compiler output (cc -S -O and scc -S -O of the sources in src/cmd and src/lib/libc, 230 files each) is input too (c:PATH).
Files of the kernel and library sources that are PLZ/ASM are not accepted by the original and are no input (some make the original run for ever).

A source that the original does not terminate on, or whose result depends on leftover memory (operr_token, operr_cc_only), is no input.
Names of labels must not be mnemonics or registers (Ld, R1, rl1 ...). Comments are /* */.
